# Keeps local dev/build artifacts out of the image "true by construction"
# rather than by accident of what happens to exist at build time. The
# Dockerfile only ever COPYs `pyproject.toml` and `src/` explicitly (never
# `COPY . .`), so nothing here can leak into the image from outside those
# two paths regardless — but anything matching below that DOES live inside
# `src/` (an editable install's build/egg-info, a stray __pycache__) would
# otherwise be swept in verbatim by `COPY src/ src/`. Mirrors .gitignore,
# but Docker does not read that file, so this one has to exist separately.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
build/
**/build/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/
